{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport hashlib\np=Path('inputs/TASK.md'); print(hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest())\nprint(p.read_text())\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport hashlib\np=Path('inputs/TASK.md'); print(hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest())\nprint(p.read_text())\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"33e08813021b43a259dc72aa35f904f82b370de25faff64488f29ee4d4495829\n# T013 matched software task: gate-result report\n\nThis is a disposable evaluation deliverable. Implement a useful, dependency-free\nPython 3.11+ command that turns one saved public formal-gate result into a faithful\nreport. It does not run or authenticate the gate, accept a representation, decide\npermission, or add a selected a_c Product feature.\n\n## Deliverable and interface\n\nCreate `gate_report.py`, `test_gate_report.py`, and `README.md` in your granted\ntask workspace. Additional local source files are allowed if useful. Use only\nthe Python standard library; no package installation, network acquisition,\nadditional model/agent invocation, or access outside the granted workspace.\nThe `inputs/` directory is immutable. Never inspect the other trial arm, hidden\nevaluation material, tenant source, proof support, credentials, or origin state.\n\nThe command is:\n\n```sh\npython3 -B gate_report.py inputs/examples/verified.json\npython3 -B -m unittest -v\n```\n\nThe first command reads the named file as exact UTF-8 bytes and writes one JSON\nreport followed by a newline to stdout. It makes no other filesystem change.\nExit 0 means a report was produced, including for a gate refusal or incomplete\ncheck. Invalid input or an unreadable file exits 2, leaves stdout empty, and gives\na concise error on stderr. No traceback is required. Do not reuse gate status\nexit codes as the report command's exit codes.\n\nThe report has exactly these top-level fields:\n\n| Field | Required content |\n| --- | --- |\n| `schema` | `t013.gate-result-report/1` |\n| `source` | Object with `raw_sha256` of the exact file bytes and `bytes`, their byte length. |\n| `reported` | The complete parsed input object, with every original field and value preserved. Preserve absence versus null, array order, exact identities, limitations, evidence and unknown extension fields. JSON whitespace/key order may change. |\n| `summary` | Object with `status`, `category`, `checked_claim_count`, and `requested_claim_count`, defined below. |\n| `cost` | Object with `elapsed_seconds`, `tokens`, and `money_usd`, defined below. |\n| `standing` | Exactly `{\"input_authenticated\": false, \"grants_authority\": false, \"establishes_semantic_acceptance\": false}`. These describe what this reporting operation establishes. |\n\nThe helper reports the saved label; it never authenticates a saved success claim.\nPreserving the full `reported` value is required even when a compact summary is\navailable. The source digest is raw-file custody, not proof of the input's truth.\n\n## Accepted input and status preservation\n\nAccept an object with `schema: \"a_c.formal-gate.result/1\"` and `status` exactly\n`verified`, `refused`, `unsupported`, or `incomplete`. Some genuine public error\noutputs have only those fields and a reason; accept them. The supplied current\ncontract and genuine retained results establish the boundary. A historical\nincomplete result is explicitly labelled as historical in custody; it is not a\nclaim that its repaired implementation defect remains current.\n\nOptional known fields have these shapes when present: `reason` is string or\nnull; `checked_claims`, `requested_claims`, and `limits` are arrays of strings;\n`inputs`, `model`, `runtime_identity`, `evidence`, `observations`, and\n`context_binding` are objects or null; `selections` is an array or null;\n`request_sha256` is string or null. Do not invent absent fields inside `reported`\nor repair their values. Unknown fields are allowed and retained. This is a\nreporting grammar, not a complete validation of a gate evidence bundle.\n\nReject malformed UTF-8, malformed JSON, duplicate object keys at any depth,\nnon-finite JSON numbers, a non-object root, unknown schema/status, and wrong\ntypes for the known fields above. Empty claim arrays are valid. Do not execute\ninput content or follow any path, URI or evidence member named by the result.\n\n`summary.status` must equal the input status exactly. Claim counts are array\nlengths when the corresponding field exists, otherwise null. No checked claim\nmay be promoted from a requested claim.\n\nUse this ordered category mapping. Comparisons with reasons are exact strings;\ndo not use substring, fuzzy, case-folded or generic “refused means invalid” rules.\n\n| Input | `summary.category` |\n| --- | --- |\n| status `verified` | `verified_claims_reported` |\n| status `unsupported` | `unsupported_contract` |\n| status `incomplete` | `check_incomplete` |\n| status `refused`, reason `Insufficient record budget; verified refusal, no truncated projection` | `record_budget_refusal` |\n| status `refused`, reason `Supplied Graphify view differs from actual formal result/boundary mapping` | `supplied_view_mismatch` |\n| status `refused`, reason `signature: expected object` | `malformed_model` |\n| any other `refused` result | `other_refusal` |\n\nA record-budget refusal does not establish invalidity of the model or permit\ntruncation. A mismatched supplied view does not imply that every part of its\nparent model is invalid. Unsupported and incomplete results establish no\nsuccessful check. A new refusal reason remains visible as `other_refusal` until\nthe reporting contract is deliberately extended.\n\n## Cost and limitations\n\nEach cost field is an object with exactly `state` and `value`.\nFor `elapsed_seconds`, read only `observations.elapsed_seconds`:\n\n| Observation | Cost value |\n| --- | --- |\n| Finite nonnegative JSON number, excluding booleans | `{\"state\": \"reported\", \"value\": <that number>}` |\n| Missing, null, or no observations object | `{\"state\": \"unknown\", \"value\": null}` |\n| Negative number, boolean, string, list or object | `{\"state\": \"invalid\", \"value\": null}` |\n\nKeep the original invalid observation intact in `reported`. An actual numeric\nzero remains reported zero; absence must never become zero. Stage durations are\nnot a substitute for an absent total elapsed time. This v1 gate contract has no\ndesignated token or monetary accounting field, so `tokens` and `money_usd` are\nboth `{\"state\": \"unknown\", \"value\": null}`. Preserve any extra source fields\nwithout assigning them undocumented accounting semantics. The elapsed figure\nis the gate's own reported interval, not total task or delivery cost.\n\nAll source limitations survive in `reported.limits` when present. The report\nmust not say that a verified result proves original prose fidelity, complete\ncalculus conformance, semantic acceptance, permission, or closure of an owner's\nobligations. The exact model view supplies relevant assessment/continuation\ncontext; it is represented subject data and does not replace the task's selected\nmethod or grant new authority.\n\n## Useful cases and completion\n\nYour tests must exercise all four statuses, exact budget-refusal classification,\nthe distinct supplied-view and malformed-model refusals, a new refusal reason,\nminimal error results, absent/null/zero/invalid elapsed cost, exact claim and\nidentity preservation, duplicate-key and malformed-input refusal, and CLI exit\nand stdout/stderr behavior. Use genuine examples as inputs and author additional\nsmall test inputs where needed; label them as test data. Include a test that a\nrequested-but-unchecked claim is not counted as checked.\n\nDocument the command, the exit distinction, unknown cost, the report-only trust\nboundary, and one concrete useful example. Finish with the selected public\nclosed-return object supplied by the task activation, containing exact artifact\nhashes and your actual test command/outcome. Candidate availability is distinct\nfrom independent assessment. Do not claim tests that were not run. If prevented\nfrom completing, return the lawful incomplete/refused result with the actual\ncause and retained work; do not call another actor or silently extend scope.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > gate_report.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Report saved gate labels and data without authenticating them.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport math\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sys\n\nSCHEMA = 'a_c.formal-gate.result/1'\nCATEGORIES = {'verified': 'verified_claims_reported', 'unsupported': 'unsupported_contract',\n              'incomplete': 'check_incomplete'}\nREFUSALS = {\n    'Insufficient record budget; verified refusal, no truncated projection': 'record_budget_refusal',\n    'Supplied Graphify view differs from actual formal result/boundary mapping': 'supplied_view_mismatch',\n    'signature: expected object': 'malformed_model',\n}\n\n\ndef unique_object(pairs):\n    result = {}\n    for key, value in pairs:\n        if key in result:\n            raise ValueError('duplicate object key')\n        result[key] = value\n    return result\n\n\ndef finite_float(value):\n    number = float(value)\n    if not math.isfinite(number):\n        raise ValueError('non-finite JSON number')\n    return number\n\n\ndef reject_constant(value):\n    raise ValueError('non-finite JSON number')\n\n\ndef make_report(raw):\n    data = json.loads(raw.decode('utf-8'), object_pairs_hook=unique_object,\n                      parse_float=finite_float, parse_constant=reject_constant)\n    if not isinstance(data, dict):\n        raise ValueError('expected object root')\n    if data.get('schema') \"'!= SCHEMA:\n        raise ValueError('\"'unknown schema')\n    status = data.get('status')\n    if not isinstance(status, str) or status not in (*CATEGORIES, 'refused'):\n        raise ValueError('unknown status')\n    shapes = {'reason': (str, type(None)), 'request_sha256': (str, type(None)),\n              'selections': (list, type(None))}\n    for key in ('inputs', 'model', 'runtime_identity', 'evidence', 'observations', 'context_binding'):\n        shapes[key] = (dict, type(None))\n    for key, types in shapes.items():\n        if key in data and not isinstance(data[key], types):\n            raise ValueError('wrong type for ' + key)\n    for key in ('checked_claims', 'requested_claims', 'limits'):\n        if key in data and (not isinstance(data[key], list) or\n                            not all(isinstance(x, str) for x in data[key])):\n            raise ValueError('expected string array for ' + key)\n    elapsed = (data.get('observations') or {}).get('elapsed_seconds')\n    state = 'unknown' if elapsed is None else 'invalid'\n    if type(elapsed) in (int, float) and elapsed >= 0:\n        state = 'reported'\n    category = CATEGORIES.get(status, REFUSALS.get(data.get('reason'), 'other_refusal'))\n    return {\n        'schema': 't013.gate-result-report/1',\n        'source': {'raw_sha256': hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest(), 'bytes': len(raw)},\n        'reported': data,\n        'summary': {'status': status, 'category': category,\n                    'checked_claim_count': len(data['checked_claims']) if 'checked_claims' in data else None,\n                    'requested_claim_count': len(data['requested_claims']) if 'requested_claims' in data else None},\n        'cost': {'elapsed_seconds': {'state': state, 'value': elapsed if state == 'reported' else None},\n                 'tokens': {'state': 'unknown', 'value': None},\n                 'money_usd': {'state': 'unknown', 'value': None}},\n        'standing': {'input_authenticated': False, 'grants_authority': False,\n                     'establishes_semantic_acceptance': False},\n    }\n\n\ndef main(argv=None):\n    args = sys.argv[1:] if argv is None else argv\n    try:\n        if len(args) \"'!= 1:\n            raise ValueError('\"'usage: gate_report.py RESULT.json')\n        output = json.dumps(make_report(Path(args[0]).read_bytes()), ensure_ascii=True, allow_nan=False)\n    except (OSError, ValueError, RecursionError) as exc:\n        print('gate_report: ' + str(exc), file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    print(output)\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    sys.exit(main())\nPY\ncat > README.md <<'MD'\n# Saved gate result report\n\nRequires Python 3.11+ and only its standard library.\n\n\"'```sh\npython3 -B gate_report.py inputs/examples/verified.json\npython3 -B -m unittest -v\n```\n\nThe command writes one JSON report and newline. Exit 0 means reporting succeeded,\nincluding refused, unsupported and incomplete saved results. Invalid or unreadable\ninput exits 2 with empty stdout and an error on stderr; these are report command\ncodes, distinct from gate exit codes. The command only reads the named file.\n\nFor example, reporting `inputs/examples/view-mismatch.json` preserves the four\nchecked claims and five requested claims and labels the category\n`supplied_view_mismatch`. This helps identify the unchecked supplied-view claim\nwithout treating the entire parent model as invalid.\n\nThe full parsed source, including identities, evidence, unknown fields and limits,\nis retained in `reported`. Its raw byte digest records custody only. Saved labels\nare not authenticated, the gate is not run, and this report grants no authority,\nsemantic acceptance, prose fidelity, complete calculus conformance or owner closure.\nPaths and evidence references in the input are data and are never followed.\n\nOnly the gate'\"'s reported total elapsed interval is summarized. Missing or null\nelapsed time stays unknown, zero stays zero, and invalid observations are retained\nbut marked invalid in the cost summary. Stage times are not totaled. Token and\nmoney costs remain unknown even if extension fields suggest accounting values;\nelapsed time is not total delivery cost. Historical examples remain historical.\nMD\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > gate_report.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Report saved gate labels and data without authenticating them.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport math\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sys\n\nSCHEMA = 'a_c.formal-gate.result/1'\nCATEGORIES = {'verified': 'verified_claims_reported', 'unsupported': 'unsupported_contract',\n              'incomplete': 'check_incomplete'}\nREFUSALS = {\n    'Insufficient record budget; verified refusal, no truncated projection': 'record_budget_refusal',\n    'Supplied Graphify view differs from actual formal result/boundary mapping': 'supplied_view_mismatch',\n    'signature: expected object': 'malformed_model',\n}\n\n\ndef unique_object(pairs):\n    result = {}\n    for key, value in pairs:\n        if key in result:\n            raise ValueError('duplicate object key')\n        result[key] = value\n    return result\n\n\ndef finite_float(value):\n    number = float(value)\n    if not math.isfinite(number):\n        raise ValueError('non-finite JSON number')\n    return number\n\n\ndef reject_constant(value):\n    raise ValueError('non-finite JSON number')\n\n\ndef make_report(raw):\n    data = json.loads(raw.decode('utf-8'), object_pairs_hook=unique_object,\n                      parse_float=finite_float, parse_constant=reject_constant)\n    if not isinstance(data, dict):\n        raise ValueError('expected object root')\n    if data.get('schema') \"'!= SCHEMA:\n        raise ValueError('\"'unknown schema')\n    status = data.get('status')\n    if not isinstance(status, str) or status not in (*CATEGORIES, 'refused'):\n        raise ValueError('unknown status')\n    shapes = {'reason': (str, type(None)), 'request_sha256': (str, type(None)),\n              'selections': (list, type(None))}\n    for key in ('inputs', 'model', 'runtime_identity', 'evidence', 'observations', 'context_binding'):\n        shapes[key] = (dict, type(None))\n    for key, types in shapes.items():\n        if key in data and not isinstance(data[key], types):\n            raise ValueError('wrong type for ' + key)\n    for key in ('checked_claims', 'requested_claims', 'limits'):\n        if key in data and (not isinstance(data[key], list) or\n                            not all(isinstance(x, str) for x in data[key])):\n            raise ValueError('expected string array for ' + key)\n    elapsed = (data.get('observations') or {}).get('elapsed_seconds')\n    state = 'unknown' if elapsed is None else 'invalid'\n    if type(elapsed) in (int, float) and elapsed >= 0:\n        state = 'reported'\n    category = CATEGORIES.get(status, REFUSALS.get(data.get('reason'), 'other_refusal'))\n    return {\n        'schema': 't013.gate-result-report/1',\n        'source': {'raw_sha256': hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest(), 'bytes': len(raw)},\n        'reported': data,\n        'summary': {'status': status, 'category': category,\n                    'checked_claim_count': len(data['checked_claims']) if 'checked_claims' in data else None,\n                    'requested_claim_count': len(data['requested_claims']) if 'requested_claims' in data else None},\n        'cost': {'elapsed_seconds': {'state': state, 'value': elapsed if state == 'reported' else None},\n                 'tokens': {'state': 'unknown', 'value': None},\n                 'money_usd': {'state': 'unknown', 'value': None}},\n        'standing': {'input_authenticated': False, 'grants_authority': False,\n                     'establishes_semantic_acceptance': False},\n    }\n\n\ndef main(argv=None):\n    args = sys.argv[1:] if argv is None else argv\n    try:\n        if len(args) \"'!= 1:\n            raise ValueError('\"'usage: gate_report.py RESULT.json')\n        output = json.dumps(make_report(Path(args[0]).read_bytes()), ensure_ascii=True, allow_nan=False)\n    except (OSError, ValueError, RecursionError) as exc:\n        print('gate_report: ' + str(exc), file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    print(output)\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    sys.exit(main())\nPY\ncat > README.md <<'MD'\n# Saved gate result report\n\nRequires Python 3.11+ and only its standard library.\n\n\"'```sh\npython3 -B gate_report.py inputs/examples/verified.json\npython3 -B -m unittest -v\n```\n\nThe command writes one JSON report and newline. Exit 0 means reporting succeeded,\nincluding refused, unsupported and incomplete saved results. Invalid or unreadable\ninput exits 2 with empty stdout and an error on stderr; these are report command\ncodes, distinct from gate exit codes. The command only reads the named file.\n\nFor example, reporting `inputs/examples/view-mismatch.json` preserves the four\nchecked claims and five requested claims and labels the category\n`supplied_view_mismatch`. This helps identify the unchecked supplied-view claim\nwithout treating the entire parent model as invalid.\n\nThe full parsed source, including identities, evidence, unknown fields and limits,\nis retained in `reported`. Its raw byte digest records custody only. Saved labels\nare not authenticated, the gate is not run, and this report grants no authority,\nsemantic acceptance, prose fidelity, complete calculus conformance or owner closure.\nPaths and evidence references in the input are data and are never followed.\n\nOnly the gate'\"'s reported total elapsed interval is summarized. Missing or null\nelapsed time stays unknown, zero stays zero, and invalid observations are retained\nbut marked invalid in the cost summary. Stage times are not totaled. Token and\nmoney costs remain unknown even if extension fields suggest accounting values;\nelapsed time is not total delivery cost. Historical examples remain historical.\nMD\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"The command now preserves the full input and reports status, claim counts, cost and standing separately. I’ll test it against the supplied examples and add cases for duplicate keys, non-finite numbers, invalid field types and CLI errors."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > test_gate_report.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Genuine retained examples plus explicitly authored test data.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport unittest\n\nfrom gate_report import make_report\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n\n\ndef authored(**fields):\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Small authored test data, not gate execution evidence.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n    return json.dumps(dict(schema='a_c.formal-gate.result/1', status='refused', **fields)).encode()\n\n\nclass ReportTests(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_genuine_examples(self):\n        expected = {'verified': ('verified', 'verified_claims_reported'),\n                    'model-only': ('verified', 'verified_claims_reported'),\n                    'budget-refusal': ('refused', 'record_budget_refusal'),\n                    'view-mismatch': ('refused', 'supplied_view_mismatch'),\n                    'malformed-model': ('refused', 'malformed_model'),\n                    'historical-incomplete': ('incomplete', 'check_incomplete'),\n                    'authored-unsupported': ('unsupported', 'unsupported_contract')}\n        for name, (status, category) in expected.items():\n            with self.subTest(name=name):\n                raw = (ROOT / 'inputs/examples' / (name + '.json')).read_bytes()\n                r = make_report(raw)\n                self.assertEqual(r['reported'], json.loads(raw))\n                self.assertEqual(set(r), {'schema', 'source', 'reported', 'summary', 'cost', 'standing'})\n                self.assertEqual(r['source'], {'raw_sha256': hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest(), 'bytes': len(raw)})\n                self.assertEqual(r['summary']['status'], status)\n                self.assertEqual(r['summary']['category'], category)\n                self.assertFalse(any(r['standing'].values()))\n\n    def test_exact_reason_and_minimal(self):\n        for reason in (None, 'new reason', 'signature: expected object ',\n                       'insufficient record budget; verified refusal, no truncated projection'):\n            r = make_report(authored(reason=reason))\n            self.assertEqual(r['summary']['category'], 'other_refusal')\n            self.assertIsNone(r['summary']['checked_claim_count'])\n        self.assertNotIn('reason', make_report(authored())['reported'])\n\n    def test_costs(self):\n        for obs in (None, {}, {'stages': [{'seconds': 10}]}, {'elapsed_seconds': None}):\n            self.assertEqual(make_report(authored(observations=obs))['cost']['elapsed_seconds'],\n                             {'state': 'unknown', 'value': None})\n        for value in (0, 0.0, 1.25, 100):\n            self.assertEqual(make_report(authored(observations={'elapsed_seconds': value}))['cost']['elapsed_seconds'],\n                             {'state': 'reported', 'value': value})\n        for value in (-1, True, False, '2', [], {}):\n            r = make_report(authored(observations={'elapsed_seconds': value}, tokens=42, money_usd=10))\n            self.assertEqual(r['reported']['observations']['elapsed_seconds'], value)\n            self.assertEqual(r['cost']['elapsed_seconds'], {'state': 'invalid', 'value': None})\n            for key in ('tokens', 'money_usd'):\n                self.assertEqual(r['cost'][key], {'state': 'unknown', 'value': None})\n\n    def test_preservation_and_unchecked(self):\n        raw = authored(checked_claims=['urn:exact:β'], requested_claims=['urn:exact:β', 'unchecked'],\n                       model={'id': ' exact identity ', 'sha256': None}, limits=['limit'],\n                       extension={'array': [None, False, 0, 'é'], 'nested': {'x': 1}})\n        r = make_report(raw)\n        self.assertEqual(r['reported'], json.loads(raw))\n        self.assertEqual(r['summary']['checked_claim_count'], 1)\n        self.assertEqual(r['summary']['requested_claim_count'], 2)\n        self.assertEqual(make_report(authored(checked_claims=[]))['summary']['checked_claim_count'], 0)\n\n    def test_invalid_inputs(self):\n        invalid = [b'\\\\xff', b'{', b'[]', b'null', b'{}', b'{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"wrong\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"refused\\\"}',\n                   b'{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.formal-gate.result/1\\\",\\\"status\\\":[]}',\n                   authored().replace(b'\\\"refused\\\"', b'\\\"new\\\"'),\n                   b'{\\\"x\\\":1,\\\"x\\\":2}', authored(extension={'x': 1}).replace(b'\\\"x\\\": 1', b'\\\"x\\\": 1, \\\"x\\\": 2')]\n        for number in (b'NaN', b'Infinity', b'-Infinity', b'1e999'):\n            invalid.append(authored(extension=0).replace(b'\\\"extension\\\": 0', b'\\\"extension\\\": ' + number))\n        for key in ('reason', 'request_sha256', 'checked_claims', 'requested_claims', 'limits',\n                    'inputs', 'model', 'runtime_identity', 'evidence', 'observations', 'context_binding', 'selections'):\n            invalid.append(authored(**{key: 42}))\n        invalid.extend([authored(checked_claims=[1]), authored(limits=None)])\n        for raw in invalid:\n            with self.subTest(raw=raw), self.assertRaises(ValueError):\n                make_report(raw)\n\n    def test_cli(self):\n        command = [sys.executable, '-B', str(ROOT / 'gate_report.py')]\n        for path in sorted((ROOT / 'inputs/examples').glob('*.json')):\n            p = subprocess.run(command + [str(path)], capture_output=True)\n            self.assertEqual(p.returncode, 0)\n            self.assertEqual(p.stderr, b'')\n            self.assertTrue(p.stdout.endswith(b'\\\\n'))\n            self.assertEqual(json.loads(p.stdout), make_report(path.read_bytes()))\n        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(dir=ROOT / 'scratch') as tmp:\n            path = Path(tmp) / 'bad.json'\n            path.write_bytes(b'{')\n            for args in ([], [str(path)], [str(Path(tmp) / 'absent')], [str(path), 'extra']):\n                p = subprocess.run(command + args, capture_output=True)\n                self.assertEqual(p.returncode, 2)\n                self.assertEqual(p.stdout, b'')\n                self.assertTrue(p.stderr)\n                self.assertNotIn(b'Traceback', p.stderr)\n            self.assertEqual(list(Path(tmp).iterdir()), [path])\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    unittest.main()\nPY\nmkdir -p support scratch\npython3 -B -m unittest -v > support/test-output.txt 2>&1\ncat support/test-output.txt\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > test_gate_report.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Genuine retained examples plus explicitly authored test data.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport unittest\n\nfrom gate_report import make_report\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n\n\ndef authored(**fields):\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Small authored test data, not gate execution evidence.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n    return json.dumps(dict(schema='a_c.formal-gate.result/1', status='refused', **fields)).encode()\n\n\nclass ReportTests(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_genuine_examples(self):\n        expected = {'verified': ('verified', 'verified_claims_reported'),\n                    'model-only': ('verified', 'verified_claims_reported'),\n                    'budget-refusal': ('refused', 'record_budget_refusal'),\n                    'view-mismatch': ('refused', 'supplied_view_mismatch'),\n                    'malformed-model': ('refused', 'malformed_model'),\n                    'historical-incomplete': ('incomplete', 'check_incomplete'),\n                    'authored-unsupported': ('unsupported', 'unsupported_contract')}\n        for name, (status, category) in expected.items():\n            with self.subTest(name=name):\n                raw = (ROOT / 'inputs/examples' / (name + '.json')).read_bytes()\n                r = make_report(raw)\n                self.assertEqual(r['reported'], json.loads(raw))\n                self.assertEqual(set(r), {'schema', 'source', 'reported', 'summary', 'cost', 'standing'})\n                self.assertEqual(r['source'], {'raw_sha256': hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest(), 'bytes': len(raw)})\n                self.assertEqual(r['summary']['status'], status)\n                self.assertEqual(r['summary']['category'], category)\n                self.assertFalse(any(r['standing'].values()))\n\n    def test_exact_reason_and_minimal(self):\n        for reason in (None, 'new reason', 'signature: expected object ',\n                       'insufficient record budget; verified refusal, no truncated projection'):\n            r = make_report(authored(reason=reason))\n            self.assertEqual(r['summary']['category'], 'other_refusal')\n            self.assertIsNone(r['summary']['checked_claim_count'])\n        self.assertNotIn('reason', make_report(authored())['reported'])\n\n    def test_costs(self):\n        for obs in (None, {}, {'stages': [{'seconds': 10}]}, {'elapsed_seconds': None}):\n            self.assertEqual(make_report(authored(observations=obs))['cost']['elapsed_seconds'],\n                             {'state': 'unknown', 'value': None})\n        for value in (0, 0.0, 1.25, 100):\n            self.assertEqual(make_report(authored(observations={'elapsed_seconds': value}))['cost']['elapsed_seconds'],\n                             {'state': 'reported', 'value': value})\n        for value in (-1, True, False, '2', [], {}):\n            r = make_report(authored(observations={'elapsed_seconds': value}, tokens=42, money_usd=10))\n            self.assertEqual(r['reported']['observations']['elapsed_seconds'], value)\n            self.assertEqual(r['cost']['elapsed_seconds'], {'state': 'invalid', 'value': None})\n            for key in ('tokens', 'money_usd'):\n                self.assertEqual(r['cost'][key], {'state': 'unknown', 'value': None})\n\n    def test_preservation_and_unchecked(self):\n        raw = authored(checked_claims=['urn:exact:β'], requested_claims=['urn:exact:β', 'unchecked'],\n                       model={'id': ' exact identity ', 'sha256': None}, limits=['limit'],\n                       extension={'array': [None, False, 0, 'é'], 'nested': {'x': 1}})\n        r = make_report(raw)\n        self.assertEqual(r['reported'], json.loads(raw))\n        self.assertEqual(r['summary']['checked_claim_count'], 1)\n        self.assertEqual(r['summary']['requested_claim_count'], 2)\n        self.assertEqual(make_report(authored(checked_claims=[]))['summary']['checked_claim_count'], 0)\n\n    def test_invalid_inputs(self):\n        invalid = [b'\\\\xff', b'{', b'[]', b'null', b'{}', b'{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"wrong\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"refused\\\"}',\n                   b'{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.formal-gate.result/1\\\",\\\"status\\\":[]}',\n                   authored().replace(b'\\\"refused\\\"', b'\\\"new\\\"'),\n                   b'{\\\"x\\\":1,\\\"x\\\":2}', authored(extension={'x': 1}).replace(b'\\\"x\\\": 1', b'\\\"x\\\": 1, \\\"x\\\": 2')]\n        for number in (b'NaN', b'Infinity', b'-Infinity', b'1e999'):\n            invalid.append(authored(extension=0).replace(b'\\\"extension\\\": 0', b'\\\"extension\\\": ' + number))\n        for key in ('reason', 'request_sha256', 'checked_claims', 'requested_claims', 'limits',\n                    'inputs', 'model', 'runtime_identity', 'evidence', 'observations', 'context_binding', 'selections'):\n            invalid.append(authored(**{key: 42}))\n        invalid.extend([authored(checked_claims=[1]), authored(limits=None)])\n        for raw in invalid:\n            with self.subTest(raw=raw), self.assertRaises(ValueError):\n                make_report(raw)\n\n    def test_cli(self):\n        command = [sys.executable, '-B', str(ROOT / 'gate_report.py')]\n        for path in sorted((ROOT / 'inputs/examples').glob('*.json')):\n            p = subprocess.run(command + [str(path)], capture_output=True)\n            self.assertEqual(p.returncode, 0)\n            self.assertEqual(p.stderr, b'')\n            self.assertTrue(p.stdout.endswith(b'\\\\n'))\n            self.assertEqual(json.loads(p.stdout), make_report(path.read_bytes()))\n        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(dir=ROOT / 'scratch') as tmp:\n            path = Path(tmp) / 'bad.json'\n            path.write_bytes(b'{')\n            for args in ([], [str(path)], [str(Path(tmp) / 'absent')], [str(path), 'extra']):\n                p = subprocess.run(command + args, capture_output=True)\n                self.assertEqual(p.returncode, 2)\n                self.assertEqual(p.stdout, b'')\n                self.assertTrue(p.stderr)\n                self.assertNotIn(b'Traceback', p.stderr)\n            self.assertEqual(list(Path(tmp).iterdir()), [path])\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    unittest.main()\nPY\nmkdir -p support scratch\npython3 -B -m unittest -v > support/test-output.txt 2>&1\ncat support/test-output.txt\"","aggregated_output":"test_cli (test_gate_report.ReportTests.test_cli) ... ok\ntest_costs (test_gate_report.ReportTests.test_costs) ... ok\ntest_exact_reason_and_minimal (test_gate_report.ReportTests.test_exact_reason_and_minimal) ... ok\ntest_genuine_examples (test_gate_report.ReportTests.test_genuine_examples) ... ok\ntest_invalid_inputs (test_gate_report.ReportTests.test_invalid_inputs) ... ok\ntest_preservation_and_unchecked (test_gate_report.ReportTests.test_preservation_and_unchecked) ... ok\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nRan 6 tests in 0.221s\n\nOK\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
